KZ3 patch 1067 (SPU pass 50; opt-in KZ3_JOIN_CUTOFF_EXIT=1): after patch 1066 a task cut off by cellSpursJoinTaskset
(parked in WAIT_SIGNAL when its taskset was joined) stays parked forever on its host thread: one leaked thread per
cut-off (pass 49: 1 cut-off in 72 joins; pass 50: 0 in 56). With the switch the cut-off task leaves the wait (Join
wakes the waiters; the 1 s timed wait catches a late one) without consuming or clearing the new generation's
SIGNALLED bit, and spu_task_cutoff_exit ends its run like a quiet halt: spu_async_run then runs the task's exit, which
1066 already makes leave the new task's bits alone, and the thread returns. Host-tested (tools/spu/test_spurs_join.sh);
no game run has exercised the exit yet, hence opt-in. "[ts-join] cut-off task N ... leaves WAIT_SIGNAL" lines (first
16, then every 64th). Upstream candidate together with 1066.

Rebased on ps3recomp v0.18.0 (SPU pass 108): upstream's coherent signal watch + 1066's parked count; 1067's `!cut` on upstream's moved signalled update.

diff --git a/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c b/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
index 8526bbb4..a24b988b 100644
--- a/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
@@ -184,6 +184,16 @@ void (*g_spu_put_hook)(uint32_t ea, uint32_t size) = 0;
  * never sees atomics); the culling probe (port/spu/kz3_cull_probe.c) watches the frame's sync word with it. */
 void (*g_kz3_putllc_hook)(uint32_t ea) = 0;
 
+/* KZ3 patch 1067: end a task cut off by cellSpursJoinTaskset from inside its WAIT_SIGNAL: back to
+ * spu_run_with_halt like a halt, without the halt's register dump; spu_async_run then runs the task's exit (which
+ * patch 1066 makes leave the new generation's bits alone) and the host thread returns. */
+void spu_task_cutoff_exit(spu_context* ctx)
+{
+    g_spu_trampoline_fn = 0;
+    if (s_spu_halt_armed) { s_spu_halt_armed = 0; longjmp(s_spu_halt_env, 1); }
+    fprintf(stderr, "[ts-join] cut-off task outside the execution driver at 0x%05X: resumes\n", ctx->pc);
+}
+
 void spu_halt(spu_context* ctx)
 {
     /* Register/context dump at halt-asserts: the WWS job's parameter guard
@@ -2615,9 +2625,10 @@ void spu_spurs_taskset_syscall(spu_context* ctx)   /* non-static: also called by
             }
             yz_lockstep_block_begin(ctx);
             spu_taskset_parked_add(ts, tid, wobj);
-            spu_taskset_wait_signal(ts, tid);
+            const int cut = spu_taskset_wait_signal(ts, tid);   /* 1 = cut off by JoinTaskset (KZ3 patch 1067) */
             spu_taskset_parked_del(ts, tid);
             yz_lockstep_block_end(ctx);
+            if (cut == 1) spu_task_cutoff_exit(ctx);   /* ends the task's run; its exit leaves the new bits alone */
             spu_ef_deliver_owed(ctx, wobj);
         }
         ctx->gpr[3]._u32[0] = 0;
